>> title: Chili con Carne
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, chiles, texas, one-pot, stew
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr
>> step.4: simmer covered 2 hr

Brown @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1/2-in dice), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{}.

Soften @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped), @garlic{6%cloves}(minced) with @&(~1)browned beef{}.

Bloom @ancho chile powder{1/4%cup}(30 g; pure ground chile, not a chili-powder blend), @ground cumin{1%Tbs}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} in @&(~1)pot{}.

Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{3%cup}(710 mL), @crushed tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g), @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} for ~{2%hr}.

Thicken @&(~1)chili{} with @masa harina{2%Tbs}(20 g; slaked in a little water).
